  (1) The DUT answered: % port1.0.1: Unsupported speed/duplex combination port1.0.1
  The auto 100 and auto 10 rows ran twice. STEP 2 read the DUT only. STEP 7 read both
  ends. Both times the DUT took 2.8 s.
  While only the DUT was forced to 100/full, the 4050 at auto read a-half a-100 (STEP 4).
  While only the 4050 was still forced to 10/full, the DUT at auto read a-half a-10 (STEP 6).
CAVEAT:  Only one copper module type was on the bench: AT-SPTXa (1000BASE-T). No other
         copper pluggable type was tested. The 4050 status and LLDP were not read during
         the `speed auto 1000`, `speed 1000` and `speed auto` rows. With both ends at auto
         (STEP 6), the 4050 read a-full a-1000. Half duplex was not tested in this case.
